-to-end, and was fully reverted each time (cmd-eb4a6214847b402c restored the original authorized_keys; final cat in cmd-b9f0ec2cfa624fb9 confirms only the original key remains). A first cleanup attempt for the backup file failed with 'Operation not permitted' (cmd-eb4a6214847b402c) but was immediately corrected with sudo (cmd-7dd1fa01705d4313), leaving no residue - confirmed by the after-executor temporary-files snapshot showing no leftover /tmp/testkey or backup files. The reboot itself (cmd-a1ef211777114fc2) is tied to the independent node-restart evidence protocol, not the public task contract, and was executed safely (background shutdown, acknowledged, boot_id change observed, services and config confirmed recovered). No unnecessary, unreverted, or unexplained mutations were found.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-eb06322ac9614f94\",\"cmd-eb4a6214847b402c\",\"cmd-7dd1fa01705d4313\",\"cmd-b9f0ec2cfa624fb9\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The task's two material outcomes - configuring opsadmin with the exact specified public key, and enforcing key-based-only SSH authentication - are both directly and convincingly demonstrated through live SSH login tests (pubkey success, password rejection) captured before and after a real reboot, with matching boot-identity, service, and file-state evidence across the transition. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also executed cleanly on the single managed node (node1), with pre-restart baseline, acknowledged restart, changed boot_id, and recovered SSH/config/account state, consistent with the fixed before/after-executor global snapshots. No residue or unresolved mutations remain.\",\"limitations\":[\"The 'after_prepare' snapshot is an alias of 'before_prepare' (prepare disabled), so preparer-vs-executor separation relies solely on comparing before_prepare to after_executor; this is sufficient here since no preparation occurred.\",\"SSH verification relied on the cluster's own management keypair as a stand-in for a generic valid key rather than the exact requested os-comparison key, since the requested key's private half is not available to the executor; this is an inherent limitation of remote verification, not a gap in the deployed configuration, which was independently confirmed byte-for-byte.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"opsadmin user exists on node1 with SSH access configured via the exact specified ed25519 public key","status":"satisfied","summary":"opsadmin user was created (cmd-b4c4b8d56e2e4fff), and /home/opsadmin/.ssh/authorized_keys was created containing exactly the requested key with correct 0700/0600 permissions and opsadmin:opsadmin ownership (cmd-deacc45b753b4405, cmd-46d6c2cc9292446f). Post-reboot re-check confirms the key content, permissions, and ownership were unchanged (cmd-e4c0eaeddb994d8a).","evidence_ids":["cmd-b4c4b8d56e2e4fff","cmd-deacc45b753b4405","cmd-46d6c2cc9292446f","cmd-e4c0eaeddb994d8a"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"SSH on node1 requires key-based authentication (password/interactive auth rejected, pubkey auth accepted) for opsadmin","status":"satisfied","summary":"sshd_config already enforced PasswordAuthentication no / PubkeyAuthentication yes (cmd-0409edc220c14deb, cmd-579dc9eec18a4563), validated with sshd -t (cmd-3ee7d8cb41924adc). This was directly confirmed with live SSH: a password/keyboard-interactive attempt against opsadmin was rejected with 'Permission denied (publickey)' (cmd-8b05f30d98e44d92), and a live login with a valid private key succeeded (cmd-eb06322ac9614f94). Both behaviors were re-verified after the reboot (cmd-b9f0ec2cfa624fb9), confirming persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0409edc220c14deb","cmd-579dc9eec18a4563","cmd-3ee7d8cb41924adc","cmd-8b05f30d98e44d92","cmd-eb06322ac9614f94","cmd-b9f0ec2cfa624fb9"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"opsadmin account has no usable password (key-only access, not merely key-preferred)","status":"satisfied","