d file-state evidence across the transition. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also executed cleanly on the single managed node (node1), with pre-restart baseline, acknowledged restart, changed boot_id, and recovered SSH/config/account state, consistent with the fixed before/after-executor global snapshots. No residue or unresolved mutations remain.","limitations":["The 'after_prepare' snapshot is an alias of 'before_prepare' (prepare disabled), so preparer-vs-executor separation relies solely on comparing before_prepare to after_executor; this is sufficient here since no preparation occurred.","SSH verification relied on the cluster's own management keypair as a stand-in for a generic valid key rather than the exact requested os-comparison key, since the requested key's private half is not available to the executor; this is an inherent limitation of remote verification, not a gap in the deployed configuration, which was independently confirmed byte-for-byte."]},"ttft_ms":15592,"type":"result","duration_ms":46515,"uuid":"0370f0fb-71b7-48ab-bb63-d895ccb7b5ad","ttft_stream_ms":1910,"time_to_request_ms":187,"first_content_frame_ms":1911,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
